   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/5n2/2pP4/3P4/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 4",
   "line": [
    "Nf6",
    "d4"
   ],
   "spoken": "The key: recapture the pawn with the knight, not the queen. Instead of exposing the queen, Black heads for a blockading knight on d5 — the dream piece against an isolated queen pawn.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Against an IQP structure, a knight recapture aiming for the d5 blockade beats an early queen sortie.",
   "plans": "Blockade d5, develop, and press the isolani."
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 42,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/5n2/3P4/3P4/8/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [
    "cxd4",
    "cxd4"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 51,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/8/3n4/3P4/8/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 6",
   "line": [
    "Nxd5"
   ],
   "spoken": "The knight lands on d5 — the ideal blockading square. This is exactly the version the side facing an isolated queen pawn dreams of: the pawn on d4 is frozen and becomes a long-term target.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "A knight blockading on d5 both stops the IQP and radiates over the whole board.",
   "plans": "Develop around the blockade and trade into a good endgame."
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 67.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/8/3n4/3P4/5N2/PP3PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 1 6",
   "line": [
    "Nf3"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 69.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp2pppp/2n5/3n4/3P4/5N2/PP3PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 2 7",
   "line": [
    "Nc6"
   ],
   "spoken": "Develop the knight to c6, adding pressure to the d4-pawn. With the rock on d5 and pieces coming out with tempo, Black is very comfortable.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Complete development while every piece leans on the isolated pawn.",
   "plans": "Pile onto d4 and keep the blockade."
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 84.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp2pppp/2n5/3n4/3P4/2N2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 3 7",
   "line": [
    "Nc3"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 14,
   "t": 122.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp3ppp/2n1p3/3n4/3P4/2N2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 0 8",
   "line": [
    "e6"
   ],
   "spoken": "The pawn to e6 solidifies the blockade — it can transpose into well-known Caro-Kann middlegame theory, and in any case leaves Black with a pleasant, safe position.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Cement the d5-blockade with e6 for a rock-solid structure.",
   "plans": "Finish development behind the fixed d5 point."
  },
